                         Poisoncraft
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Extract a suitable corpse for one recipe reagent, then prepare that
reagent into a persistent dose:

  extract <corpse>
  prepare <poison> [count]
  poison <poison> [on <weapon>]
  envenom <weapon> with <poison>

A coating is runtime-only. It lasts for three landed delivery attempts
or fifteen minutes, and consumes a charge even if the victim resists.
It is never saved on the weapon. Effects and damage belong to whoever
is wielding the weapon when it lands. A victim can carry no more than
two distinct Thief poison effects. Reapplying one refreshes the
stronger effect; a third distinct poison expires the oldest.

Use 'envenomstrike <target>' in combat to spend one Opportunity and
force a coating delivery attempt at reduced direct damage.

Recipes: greenbite, widows_kiss, grave_milk, nerve_lace, black_lotus,
throatdust, glassblood, dreamrot, and nightshade. Recipes open every
two Thief Ranks from 3 through 19. Glassblood uses common Bleeding.

Forced NPC dosing uses 'lace <poison> into <npc>' on a suitable local
intelligent NPC. At Rank 16, the same command can lace a deployed pressure
trap: 'lace <poison> into trap'.
